          "ihh:quote": "1867\nApril 21 : John Muir turns 29 years old\nMarch 5 : Blinded in a factory accident. After weeks of agony, cared for by Catharine Merrill, his sight returns. Muir decides to leave factory work to study nature.",
          "ihh:locator": "1867"
        },
        {
          "ihh:source": {
            "@id": "ihh:MUI-S-0023"
          },
          "ihh:quote": "1867 Temporarily blinded by eye injury. Once his sight is restored, decides to commit his life to nature study.",
          "ihh:locator": "1867"
        },
        {
          "ihh:source": {
            "@id": "ihh:MUI-S-0019"
          },
          "ihh:quote": "He then went to work in a factory in Indianapolis where he worked his way up until 1867 when he had an accident that left him temporarily blind. The shock and horror of the accident for Muir finally pushed him to leave industry work forever.",
          "ihh:locator": "paragraph 3"
        }
      ],
