          "ihh:source": {
            "@id": "ihh:MUI-S-0024"
          },
          "ihh:quote": "1914\nApril 21 : John Muir turns 76 years old\nMay: A young Japanese college student, Ryozo Azuma, learns about Muir when visiting Mt. Rainier from Tacoma Washington's College of the Pacific; he reads Muir's books and travels to Martinez where he meets Muir. Azuma later becomes a noted Japanese conservationist and mountaineer, known as \"The John Muir of Japan.\"\nDecember 24 : John Muir dies in California Hospital, Los Angeles, from pneumonia on Christmas eve",
          "ihh:locator": "1914"
        }
