            "@id": "ihh:MUI-S-0024"
          },
          "ihh:quote": "Muir's seventh trip to Alaska, with the Harriman Alaska Expedition to Wrangell, Glacier Bay, Sitka, Prince William Sound, and the Aleutian Islands and beyond. In 1899, railroad magnate Edward H. Harriman organized a summer voyage to the wilds of Alaska: He converted a steamship, the George W. Elder, into a luxury \"floating university,\" populated by some of America's best and brightest scientists and writers, including John Muir. Those aboard encountered",
