      "ihh:notes": "Artifacts research 2026-10-20: the two images named 'Name: John Muir; Age/Year of Birth: 1838' in this volume (objectIds 235846729 and 235846730; 0420.jpg 3308x6001, 0421.jpg 3360x5961). Rights from the volume's useRestriction.status in MUI-S-0072. Read by eye on 2026-10-20, NOT facts (no transcription exists): sworn at Martinez, County of Contra Costa, 28 April 1903, stamped Passport Bureau May 5 1903; born at Dunbar, Scotland, 21 April 1838; emigrated with his parents in March 1849, sailing from Glasgow in the ship 'Warren' on or about 2 March 1849; naturalized 28 April 1903 before the Superior Court of Contra Costa County; occupation botanist and geology. Needs a human transcription (or a Citizen Archivist transcription) to become facts; this is the Warren ship lead. Stops 1-2 (emigration) and 6 (Martinez).\nAuthorship set on 2026-10-20: private (John Muir) (private-writings rule, DECISIONS 2026-10-20): John Muir's own passport application.\nEdit lock (2026-10-20): rights fields changed after verification; adversary verdict 'supported' by codex:gpt-6.1-sol (run adv-20261020T170152-278c, 2026-10-20) cleared for re-verification."
