      "description": "Closest wording, none states the full claim on its own: Pacific chronology (registered university-of-the-pacific) has '1871 September First article on glaciers sent to New York Tribune' (says sent, not written or published). Sierra Club Yosemite Glaciers page: published in the Tribune December 5, 1871 as his first published work, datelined September 28th, 1871 (date of writing must be inferred from the dateline). Swett 1893 sketch: his first article on the Yosemite glaciers was written in the sawmill study and published in the Tribune in 1871 (no September). Bade ch. 9: in September 1871 he sent the first of several serial letters to the Tribune, which appeared December 5th 1871 as 'Yosemite Glaciers' (first Tribune letter, not first article for publication). None contradicts the claim; no source staged."
